import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a5 as r}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Implementation plan — backend video editing","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/server-video-editor/plan.md","filePath":"feature/server-video-editor/plan.md"}'),i={name:"feature/server-video-editor/plan.md"};function n(s,e,d,l,c,p){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="implementation-plan-—-backend-video-editing" tabindex="-1">Implementation plan — backend video editing <a class="header-anchor" href="#implementation-plan-—-backend-video-editing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Implementation plan — backend video editing&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Spec: spec.md. User authorization is implementation of this backend workflow and extra video/voice inputs, using existing infrastructure. Local test/deployment package first; no VM account currently available.</p><h2 id="global-constraints" tabindex="-1">Global constraints <a class="header-anchor" href="#global-constraints" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Global constraints&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use isolated worktrees seeded from dirty root source. No commit/push. Existing Video Space and product generation remain compatible. No paid footage generation. LLM never executes code; immutable/private assets only. Reuse FFmpeg/Pillow/NumPy/faster-whisper/edge-tts already installed, existing licensed media/font and existing credit helper. Do not add multiple rendering frameworks. Do not alter DemoVideo/Viro source. Update central docs in spec→plan→task→test order when contracts change.</p><h2 id="task1-portable-ai-worker-and-full-editorial-resources" tabindex="-1">Task1: portable AI worker and full editorial resources <a class="header-anchor" href="#task1-portable-ai-worker-and-full-editorial-resources" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Task1: portable AI worker and full editorial resources&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Own worktree <code>brandhub-ai-service</code>. Read spec and an exact task brief before implementing. Files: <code>app/models/server_video_edit_models.py</code>; <code>app/services/server_video_edit/{analysis,planner,renderer,service,store,media}.py</code> split only by responsibility; <code>app/api/v1/endpoints/server_video_edit.py</code>; minimal proxy/config/router; standalone <code>app/video_edit_worker.py</code>; packaged resources under <code>app/resources/video-edit/</code> and <code>tools/video-edit/</code>; worker Dockerfile/requirements/env/example docs/tests. No Business/Web changes.</p><p>Implement exact internal source envelope/API from spec; final Python model defines <code>plan</code> returned/passed unchanged. Send final response/model schema to controller before downstream task. Mongo journal uses <code>video_edit_executions</code> and no TTL; reuse product Mongo lease semantics through configurable collection or focused adapter, no existing collection migration. File/provider helpers permit local fixture injection only in tests, never public arbitrary paths. S3 hashing, ownership-derived keys, process timeouts and queue bounds mandatory.</p><p>Review ruling: internal plan POST is asynchronous202 and has GET <code>/plans/{job_id}</code>. Persist provider-start fence; ambiguous Claude crash/timeout is RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED, never call again automatically. Source plan scope active scene and120000ticks/sec. Reject unsupported content, retain manual base. QC numeric gates in spec.</p><p>Plan/render pipeline: source probe and bounded sampled frames; optional transcript/TTS through actual mounted tools/config; Claude minimized multimodal context plus bundled guides; strict plan validation (all referenced IDs, bounded geometry and full source timing); renderer implements genre-appropriate compositing/FFmpeg graph from typed values, never model strings. Full final decode/frame+audio QC and output checksum precede completion. Include per-stage progress and restart-safe render receipt. Standalone worker has only video dependencies, reads env normally, never <code>.env</code> file copying or keys in output. Existing AI API forwards internal <code>/video-edit/*</code> to configured worker URL, default localhost8094 for local integration.</p><p>Transport ruling after code audit: existing private originals use app envelope encryption. Worker must fetch only fixed Business internal job/asset routes and use Business output-session/complete capabilities for output, never direct S3 plaintext reads/writes. Envelope omits object_key; see updated spec. Business media receives/validates/decrypts and counts quota. Do not copy AES/storage credentials to worker. Reuse verified cached output after upload interruptions. Tests first for schema boundary/malformed/foreign refs/path/NaN/budget; offline Claude fixtures and real FFmpeg synthetic composition. Run current video/caption relevant regressions once. Deliver exact changed-file manifest, model schema/API examples and truthful capability table. No subagents/paid calls/live DB/S3 calls.</p><h2 id="task2-business-owner-scoped-auto-edit-orchestration" tabindex="-1">Task2: Business owner-scoped auto-edit orchestration <a class="header-anchor" href="#task2-business-owner-scoped-auto-edit-orchestration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Task2: Business owner-scoped auto-edit orchestration&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Own Business worktree. New <code>VideoAutoEditService</code> + <code>VideoAutoEditStore</code> Mongo documents/controllers or extend existing VideoProjectController. Build source descriptors solely from accepted snapshot/READY assets in <code>VideoMediaStore</code>; provider must be configured S3 and immutable hash/size present. Expected revision checked on first admission; persist an immutable snapshot/source branch. Later manual revisions do not overwrite or cancel that separate output. Same-key replay resolves the original job before reading the latest snapshot. Stable job UUID based scoped Idempotency-Key; plan invocation through <code>AiCreditGenerationService</code> new internal Action and CONTENT_GENERATE with payload identity, no new pricing. Internal proxy call <code>/api/v1/ai/video-edit/plan</code> yields usable <code>{job_id,summary,plan}</code>; validated output persists in normal accounting replay. Submit unchanged plan to worker via AiServiceClient <code>/video-edit/jobs</code>; get status via that same internal proxy. Store owner/revision/job fingerprint with majority write concern; no DB transaction spans HTTP. Same key+same revision/instruction must recover partially acknowledged submit; no second paid plan. New key creates separate job and never overwrites originals.</p><p>Review correction to above synchronous wording: public POST returns durable202 before heavy work. Reserve existing CONTENT_GENERATE through existing accounting/prepare at submission, then durable Business dispatcher handles PLANNING/PLANNED/SUBMITTING/RENDERING. New async planning Action records WAITING on accepted worker plan job and settles only when GET plan receipt is completed+valid; known failed/no usable plan finishes0; ambiguous outcome stays held/reconciliation-required. Reconcile by same stable job ID via GET, never generic UNKNOWN replay that would strand a job or blind Claude retry. If initial worker admission is definitively404, replay the same ID is safe because worker requires durable journal before provider. Cross-store interrupted submissions are recovered by scoped key; no second reserve/provider call. No DB transaction spans network.</p><p>Expose exact public API and fixed internal source/output transport from spec; stream output only after owned completed receipt via existing VideoMediaVerifier/decrypt. Include GET <code>/auto-edits</code> list for resume. Enforce project ownership for list/get/content (not just workspace membership). Media upload current encryption/inventory/provider guards remain, investigate readiness rather than bypass encrypted reads. No direct user storage URL or token. Add focused API/service/accounting/access tests. No live DB/cloud writes. Send exact response/error shape/changed manifest to controller. No subagents/commit/push.</p><h2 id="task3-native-assistant-host-integration" tabindex="-1">Task3: native assistant/host integration <a class="header-anchor" href="#task3-native-assistant-host-integration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Task3: native assistant/host integration&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Own Web worktree. Reuse <code>vendor/video-space/src/brandhub/studio-controls.tsx</code> and edit-session/sync, exact protocol whitelist (<code>shared/video-space-protocol.ts</code>), host service/bridge, errors and native vi/en messages. Add <code>Dựng tự động trên máy chủ</code> using same instruction; save current project first, send expected revision, show async job stages, poll/list previous jobs when reopening, authorize download via host blob and let user save MP4. Keep existing 8-action assistant and original timeline. Host postAiWithCredit for POST with route workspace; strict GET list/status/content path patterns. Reuse token-free iframe protocol. No external fetch URL, no auth propagation to provider URLs.</p><p>Local verification tests under tests/ only. Host protocol/service tests, native session states, actual browser fixture queued→progress→completed→download, vi/en dark/light and existing manual editor smoke. Required npm ci once final scope stable, typecheck native separately; do not expand unrelated UI. Add worker-env/deployment wiring to infra in controller.</p><h2 id="controller-integration-and-proof" tabindex="-1">Controller integration and proof <a class="header-anchor" href="#controller-integration-and-proof" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Controller integration and proof&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Three tasks execute sequentially under subagent-driven-development; controller owns requirements/interface decisions and final review. Hash-guard copy changed files only back to root; keep prior changes. Run worker local fixture with generated media and real render+QC; then configure runtime key/URI via ignored env and verify actual authenticated public plan/job/status/content with low-cost Claude once if required (no new footage). Private media upload can use own small test file through normal workflow; don&#39;t bypass quota/encryption. Package standalone Linux VM deployment and explicit model-volume/config preflight. Review final source before reporting; no claim VM deployed.</p><h2 id="_2026-11-11-—-editable-export-implementation" tabindex="-1">2026-11-11 — Editable export implementation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-11-—-editable-export-implementation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-11 — Editable export implementation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Reuse RenderPlan with an optional editable boolean defaulting false, passed through existing Business JSON storage and ownership checks. Give Claude the schema and a source/library manifest; require TIMELINE.json with real original clip cuts, native text and audio layers. Validate sidecar against envelope and verified probes and compare its geometry to the produced MP4. Keep legacy geometry-only results compatible. Native chat branches on editable: feed actual plan and existing project media to renderPlanScene; otherwise preserve flattened MP4 import. Extend importer to independent source-video audio tracks, music trim/speed and packaged SFX through existing library assets; disclose unsupported effects and server-save failures. Touch worker model/claude_code and tests; native auto-edit-chat/import-render-plan/studio-messages and tests; add the packaged SFX files during library build using bundled worker resources. No new dependency, no Business API or ownership changes, no commits or paid calls.</p><h2 id="_2026-11-11-—-missing-editor-resources" tabindex="-1">2026-11-11 — Missing editor resources <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-11-—-missing-editor-resources" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-11 — Missing editor resources&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use new UploadedAudioView under existing Audio switch, subscribe to editor.media assets and reuse processMediaAssets/useFileUpload/buildElementFromMedia. Fix missing effect preview image and subpath URL; add real presets using existing color-adjust/gaussian-blur shaders and register once. Localized resource messages; use existing themed controls. Add native data regressions and browser fixtures covering upload/play/add/save/reload, filter replace/clear/Undo and effects parameter/render behavior.</p>',23)])])}const h=o(i,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,h as default};
